  numeric_list_result_reverse_sort
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated list of numbers is asked to be sorted from largest to smallest without a request for code"
    effect "the list is restated in descending order"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "5, 2, 9, 1 sorted in descending order: 9, 5, 2, 1."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  numeric_list_result_reverse
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated list of numbers is asked to be reversed without a request for code"
    effect "the list is restated in reverse order"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "5, 2, 9, 1 in reverse order: 1, 9, 2, 5."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  number_primality_prime
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated whole number above the trial-division threshold is asked whether it is prime and it is"
    effect "the number is confirmed prime with the trial-division bound that no divisor reaches"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Yes, 97 is a prime number: no integer from 2 to 9 divides it."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  number_primality_prime_small
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated small whole number is asked whether it is prime and it is"
    effect "the number is confirmed prime by naming its only divisors"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "Yes, 7 is a prime number: its only divisors are 1 and 7."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  number_primality_composite
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated whole number is asked whether it is prime and it has a proper factor"
    effect "the number is declared composite with its smallest factor and cofactor"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "No, 91 is not a prime number: 91 = 7 x 13, so 7 divides it."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  number_primality_below_two
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a stated whole number below two is asked whether it is prime"
    effect "the number is declared not prime by restating that a prime is greater than 1"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "No, 1 is not a prime number: a prime is a whole number greater than 1."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-quantities.lino"
  meta_explanation_why
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "the user asks why the previous answer was given"
    effect "the answer names the deterministic Links Notation rule that matched and points at the appended evidence and trace"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "I answered that way because the prompt matched a deterministic Links Notation rule."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino"
  how_it_works_prior_topic
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a how-does-it-work question names a term known only from the prior conversation"
    effect "the answer admits no mechanism rule exists for the term yet and asks for a Links Notation fact describing it"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "To explain how the term works I need a Links Notation fact with the mechanism description."
    grounding "data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino"
  how_it_works_no_context
    defined-by answer
    role localized_response_template
    precondition "a how-does-it-work follow-up names no topic and the conversation supplies none"
    effect "the answer explains the matched rule and suggests asking about a concrete known concept"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "To ask about a specific topic, try how does X work where X is a concept I know."
